From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:05:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: fail fast on big-page sysmem attempts that RM retries
 itself

Two RM-internal sysmem allocations try big pages first and fall back to
smaller pages on NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY:

- sysmemConstruct() with NVOS32_ATTR_PAGE_SIZE_DEFAULT on GPUs that
  allow large default sysmem pages walks down the page sizes with
  _sysmemGetNextSmallestPageSize().
- _kgmmuClientShadowFaultBufferPagesAllocate() asks for huge pages
  and retries with RM_PAGE_SIZE (Bug 5042223). This runs every time a
  UVM client registers a GPU.

Set MEMDESC_FLAGS_ALLOC_FAIL_FAST on these attempts so that they don't
stall in direct reclaim and compaction when memory is fragmented. The
last attempt uses the smallest page size, which is an order-0
allocation and keeps __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL either way; the shadow fault
buffer clears the flag before its retry to make that explicit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 57486605d761809ed40501b9163c1c6bf47dfd1e)
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mmu/kern_gmmu.c  | 4 +++-
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mmu/kern_gmmu.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mmu/kern_gmmu.c
index a1fcfb37..56169d1d 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mmu/kern_gmmu.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mmu/kern_gmmu.c
@@ -1606,7 +1606,8 @@ _kgmmuClientShadowFaultBufferPagesAllocate
     NV_STATUS status;
     GMMU_CLIENT_SHADOW_FAULT_BUFFER *pClientShadowFaultBuffer;
     MEMORY_DESCRIPTOR *pMemDesc;
-    NvU64 flags = MEMDESC_FLAGS_NONE;
+    // The huge page attempt below falls back to small pages.
+    NvU64 flags = MEMDESC_FLAGS_ALLOC_FAIL_FAST;
     NvU32 shadowFaultBufferSizeTotal;
 
     //
@@ -1642,6 +1643,7 @@ _kgmmuClientShadowFaultBufferPagesAllocate
     {
         NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR, "Allocation failed with big page size, retrying with default page size\n");
         memdescSetPageSize(pMemDesc, AT_GPU, RM_PAGE_SIZE);
+        memdescSetFlag(pMemDesc, MEMDESC_FLAGS_ALLOC_FAIL_FAST, NV_FALSE);
         memdescTagAlloc(status, NV_FB_ALLOC_RM_INTERNAL_OWNER_UNNAMED_TAG_33, pMemDesc);
     }
 
diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c
index 2dc8f00d..e2374fdd 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c
@@ -335,6 +335,10 @@ sysmemConstruct_IMPL
 
         memdescSetFlag(pMemDesc, MEMDESC_FLAGS_SYSMEM_OWNED_BY_CLIENT, NV_TRUE);
 
+        // A failed attempt is retried below with the next smaller page size.
+        if (bRetry)
+            memdescSetFlag(pMemDesc, MEMDESC_FLAGS_ALLOC_FAIL_FAST, NV_TRUE);
+
         if ((sysGetStaticConfig(SYS_GET_INSTANCE()))->bOsCCEnabled &&
             gpuIsCCFeatureEnabled(pGpu) 
             && FLD_TEST_DRF(OS32, _ATTR2, _MEMORY_PROTECTION, _UNPROTECTED,
